  "$comment": "Golden vectors for the coordinator.v1 facet-key grammar (sync.proto rule 6, 0.3.0; the import's keys, import.proto THE SERVER DECIDES). Every implementation (this package's parsers and builders, fc-coordinator's Push validation, fc-mobile's store) must agree with every case. Ids are lowercase dashed uuids; `default` is legal only as a collection id; kinds are owned | ordered | wished | former. `valid` keys parse to exactly one family, user- or server-owned; `invalid` keys parse to none (a Push of one is REJECTED facet_key_not_user_owned). `build` folds case; `buildRejects` throw. `mfcIds` are the canonical MFC ids (leading zeros stripped, 1 to 64 ASCII digits; canonicalMfcId) and the ones refused. `mfcImportOccIds` are importOccIdFromMac(HMAC-SHA256(key, name)), the ids the MFC import gives each copy, minted here under `mfcImportOccTestKey`: a PUBLISHED TEST key that is never the production key, which the coordinator alone holds.",
